    "highlights": [
      "California's price level is the highest of 51 states and DC, so labor, permits and extras cost more here than almost anywhere: about $720 of labor on a gas tank against $650 nationally.",
      "Electricity is expensive in California (31.35 cents per kWh, the 2nd highest), so a standard electric tank costs about $910 a year to run and a heat pump saves about $687 a year against it.",
      "Natural gas costs more here than in most states ($2.15 per therm, the 4th highest), so gas's running-cost advantage is smaller than the national picture suggests.",
      "78% of California homes heat water with natural gas, against 48% nationally, so most replacements here are gas-to-gas with an existing vent and gas line.",
      "Where you live inside California matters: the same 50-gallon gas job is about $1,951 in the San Francisco-Oakland-Fremont, CA area and $1,868 in the Riverside-San Bernardino-Ontario, CA area.",
      "California requires earthquake straps."
    ]
  },
